<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><strong>Diarmuid Early</strong>, dubbed the =
=E2=80=9CLebron James=E2=80=9D of competitive Excel, remembers it well. Whe=
n he worked at the Boston Consulting Group in 2008, he=E2=80=99d have a ste=
ady stream of people by his desk every Friday waiting to ask him questions =
about Excel and peek at any custom formulas he might have handy.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">Now, things appear to be changing.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%"><br>Major Wall Street banks are <a href=3D"ht=
tps://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWySsF7CZgnXW3xydQk7GQhy7W4=
