"LskPn4mJ" target=3D"_blank">Morgan Stanley</a> analysis using BLS data fou=
nd that the number of Americans employed as bookkeepers and accounting cler=
ks fell from about <strong>2m</strong> to <strong>1.5m</strong> between 198=
7 and 2002.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">However, more analytical roles like those of =
financial managers and management analysts went up (from <strong>600k</stro=
ng> to <strong>1.5m</strong>) over that same time period.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:125%">In other words, Excel didn=E2=80=99t eliminat=
e jobs so much as create demand for new ones.</p></div></div></td></tr></tb=
